Subject: [PATCH] riscv: idle: CONFIG option to never execute wfi (SoCLabs MBV wfi-coma workaround)

Config-gated variant of the linux_soc unconditional workaround patch
(../../linux_soc/linux/patches/linux/0002-*): the wfi-coma behaviour is a
property of bitstreams built with C_INTERRUPT_WAKEUP=0 (silicon-proven
2026-07-16, repro src/linux_soc/fw_mspin). The shell_linux transplant BD
pins + asserts C_INTERRUPT_WAKEUP=1, so the harness ships BOTH idle
variants until that bitstream is silicon-proven:

  Image        (RISCV_SOCLABS_NOWFI_IDLE=n)  stock wfi idle
  Image_nowfi  (RISCV_SOCLABS_NOWFI_IDLE=y)  busy-poll idle

Default n: byte-for-byte the stock idle path unless the option is set.

--- linux-6.18.7.orig/arch/riscv/Kconfig	2026-01-23 10:21:37.000000000 +0000
+++ linux-6.18.7/arch/riscv/Kconfig	2026-07-16 22:15:11.348698339 +0100
@@ -1146,6 +1146,24 @@
 
           If unsure, say N.
 
+config RISCV_SOCLABS_NOWFI_IDLE
+	bool "Never execute WFI in the idle loop (SoCLabs MBV wfi-coma workaround)"
+	default n
+	help
+	  Workaround for AMD MicroBlaze-V silicon built with
+	  C_INTERRUPT_WAKEUP=0, where a hart in WFI is a coma: no interrupt
+	  and no debug halt ever wakes it (SoCLabs linux_soc fw_mspin
+	  discriminator, 2026-07-16 -- the same interrupts deliver perfectly
+	  into a busy loop). With this option the kernel idle path returns
+	  immediately instead of sleeping; the generic idle loop then
+	  busy-polls with IRQs enabled between iterations, exactly like the
+	  generic "nohlt" mode.
+
+	  Say N on hardware whose MicroBlaze-V was built with
+	  C_INTERRUPT_WAKEUP=1 (the shell_linux transplant BD pins and
+	  asserts this) and on qemu-virt. Say Y only for bitstreams whose
+	  WFI wake-up is unproven or known broken.
+
 endmenu # "Kernel features"
 
 menu "Boot options"
--- linux-6.18.7.orig/arch/riscv/include/asm/cpuidle.h	2026-01-23 10:21:37.000000000 +0000
+++ linux-6.18.7/arch/riscv/include/asm/cpuidle.h	2026-07-16 22:15:11.351698599 +0100
@@ -12,6 +12,21 @@
 
 static inline void cpu_do_idle(void)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_RISCV_SOCLABS_NOWFI_IDLE
+	/*
+	 * SoCLabs MBV wfi-coma silicon workaround (see the Kconfig help):
+	 * never execute wfi in the idle path. Return immediately with the
+	 * IRQ state unchanged (still disabled, per the arch_cpu_idle()
+	 * contract); default_idle_call() then re-enables interrupts, any
+	 * pending IRQ is taken, and do_idle() re-checks need_resched() --
+	 * i.e. the CPU busy-polls exactly like the generic "nohlt" mode.
+	 *
+	 * Other wfi sites are deliberately left alone: they are only in
+	 * post-panic/halt parking loops and SMP secondary paths that a
+	 * single-hart system never executes at runtime.
+	 */
+	cpu_relax();
+#else
 	/*
 	 * Add mb() here to ensure that all
 	 * IO/MEM accesses are completed prior
@@ -19,6 +34,7 @@
 	 */
 	mb();
 	wait_for_interrupt();
+#endif
 }
 
 #endif
